 {"id":"fabro-c16d","title":"sd CLI default --limit 50 silently hides goal-mandated seeds from the planner","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T21:19:45.207Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T21:19:45.207Z","description":"Adopted from run 01M1PVMS7B6N39MG0041C5F7P6 planner painpoint.\n\n## Failure\n\n`sd ready` and `sd list` both default to `--limit 50`. After the tracker consolidation (109 open seeds, ~50 High), the goal-mandated seed fabro-8822 (priority 2) was truncated out of BOTH listings — the seed looked absent until the planner retried with `--limit 200`.\n\n## Fix directions\n\n- develop planner prompt (this repo, .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md sd reference): pin `--limit 200` on tracker listings — partially adopted 2026-09-04.\n- upstream seeds CLI: warn when output is truncated by the limit (external repo, @os-eco/seeds-cli).\n- tracker hygiene: keep open-seed count under the limit (priority discipline).\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA goal naming a priority-2 seed resolves via `sd` listings without manual limit guessing.","labels":["workflows","painpoint-adopted"]}
 {"id":"fabro-27f9","title":"unexplained: .fabro/project.toml truncated to 0 bytes at 2026-09-04 23:08 (no identified writer)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T21:38:06.823Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T21:38:06.823Z","description":"## Failure (observed 2026-09-04)\n\nDuring the closeout-stdin diagnosis window, .fabro/project.toml was truncated to 0 bytes on the denkhaus working tree (mtime 2026-09-04 23:08:02 +0200, between commits cef7c2497 20:19 and f7db7d05a 23:10 — the slimmed 505-byte content was committed and intact before, gone after). No recurrence after restore (checked again ~23:37 and later); the file holds the slim project-root content.\n\nRuled out by reproduction (file stayed 505 bytes): `nu closeout.nu` (with sd shim), `fabro ps`, `fabro validate develop`, `fabro preflight develop`. Ruled out by timing: `fabro run` create (23:20) and `just up` rebuild window. Candidates not yet excluded: an interrupted IPython cell in that window, the edit skill, mise activation side effects.\n\n## Impact if it recurs\n\nA zero-byte project.toml still parses (empty layer) but silently breaks project discovery semantics; a run create from such a tree warns about the dirty worktree.\n\n## Fix\n\nIf it recurs: run the watcher (`stat` poll loop) or inotify on the file, capture the writing PID (fanotify/auditd), and check whether any fabro-config write path can open project.toml O_TRUNC (grep for `File::create` near project config). Watcher was prepared but not running when last checked.","labels":["platform","painpoint-adopted"]}
